Emerging Market Opportunities
Investment in green hydrogen production and advanced electrolysis systems is creating new opportunities for specialised titanium anodes. Manufacturers are developing iridium-based and mixed oxide coatings designed to support demanding electrochemical operating conditions.

Advanced coating technologies, including improved thermal decomposition processes and surface engineering, may enhance electrode durability while optimising precious metal consumption. Growing demand for high-performance water treatment and metal recovery systems also offers additional opportunities.

Regional Market Insights
Asia-Pacific dominated the global market in 2025, accounting for an estimated 42% share. Strong chemical manufacturing activity, electroplating demand, and investment in water treatment infrastructure support the region's leading position.

North America represents an established market, with demand from chemical processing, pipeline protection, and specialised industrial applications. Europe benefits from its electrochemical manufacturing base and advanced environmental treatment requirements. South America and the Middle East and Africa offer opportunities through mining, desalination, and oil and gas infrastructure projects.

